      "content": "You raise a compelling point that the pursuit of truth over reassurance should indeed be the core of rigorous history education. While \"shared values\" can sometimes be a rhetorical convenience, historically valid narratives about power and inequality are actually the most accurate way to construct a meaningful sense of collective identity. True accuracy includes acknowledging pain and conflict, which paradoxically builds a more resilient and truthful understanding of unity than a simplified version of it ever could.",
